# ── Round 2 (2026-07-19, run 29703790765 -> re-scan of embedded-amd64-r174)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ground truth: a real `trivy image --ignorefile .trivyignore --format json`
# scan of ghcr.io/pleme-io/pangea-operator:embedded-amd64-r174-5ad8c29 (the
# image built by the magma dependency bump in 5ad8c29, the first commit
# after Round 1's 39c76c3) — 26 findings (2 CRITICAL / 10 HIGH / 13 MEDIUM /
# 1 LOW), none of them already covered by the 45 entries above (confirmed:
# none of the 26 finding IDs matched an existing line in this file before
# this round's additions). None of these are caused by the magma bump
# itself -- magma is a pure-Rust dependency with zero overlap with the
# opentofu/packer/terraform-provider-kubernetes Go binaries or the
# pangea-aws/pangea-core Ruby gemsets below. 6 of the 26 (concurrent-ruby,
# CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM) were a REAL, FIXED gap in Round 1's own remediation
# (see pangea-aws and pangea-core commits, same day) -- Round 1 bumped only
# THIS repo's pangea-compiler/gemset.nix, missing that pangea-aws and
# pangea-core (embedded into this image as RUBYLIB path-gems with their
# OWN checked-in vendor/bundle, resolved from their OWN Gemfile.lock) each
# vendor an independent copy of the same vulnerable concurrent-ruby 1.3.6.
# The remaining 20 (17 unique IDs below) are genuinely-unfixable residuals
# in opentofu/packer/terraform-provider-kubernetes, the same three binaries
# Round 1 already bumped via the nixpkgs-security escape hatch -- verified
# 2026-07-19 that opentofu v1.12.4, packer v1.15.4, and
# terraform-provider-kubernetes v3.2.1 are EACH the latest tagged release
# on their GitHub repo (checked both `releases/latest` and `tags`) AND the
# latest version packaged by nixpkgs-security's own nixos-unstable pin --
# there is no newer package to bump to.

# opentofu 1.12.4 -- go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk v1.42.0 (CVE-2026-39883,
# HIGH) and the otlp{log,metric,trace}http exporters v1.42.0/v0.18.0
# (CVE-2026-39882, MEDIUM, on 3 separate exporter packages). Checked
# opentofu's own `main` branch go.mod directly (not just the latest
# release): otel/sdk is ALREADY bumped to v1.44.0 and the otlp exporters to
# v1.44.0/v0.20.0 there -- the fix is real and written, just not yet cut
# into a tagged release (latest tag v1.12.4, 2026-07-13, predates that
# main-branch bump). No nixpkgs packaging exists for an untagged commit,
# and building opentofu from an unreleased git rev is out of scope for
# this pass (no reachable x86_64-linux builder from this workstation to
# verify the resulting binary). Re-check when opentofu cuts its next tag.
CVE-2026-39883
CVE-2026-39882

